# SecurePharma — Project Structure Rules

> Always apply on every file operation. These rules define WHERE new code/config/docs must live so the repo stays clean and consistent.

## 1. Top-level layout (do not break)

```
SecurePharma/
├── backend/                # Node.js + Express API (MUST stay here)
├── frontend/               # React + Vite client   (MUST stay here)
├── docs/                   # ALL project documentation (.md) — NOT root
│   ├── README.md           # Index of docs/ folder
│   ├── *.md                # Living docs (plan, features, install, …)
│   └── archive/            # Completed/obsolete phase checklists
├── .cursor/rules/          # Cursor rules (this folder)
├── .agents/skills/         # Agent skills (read-only reference)
├── README.md               # Single entry point at repo root ONLY
├── .env                    # Backend env (NEVER commit secrets)
├── .gitignore
└── package.json            # Workspace root only if multi-package; otherwise backend/ or frontend/
```

## 2. Markdown / documentation placement

**HARD RULE:** `.md` files are NOT allowed at repo root except `README.md`.

| File type | Where it goes |
|---|---|
| Project entry point / overview | `./README.md` (root, single file) |
| Living docs (plan, features, install, ADR, RFC, guide) | `./docs/<NAME>.md` |
| Completed phase checklist / obsolete doc | `./docs/archive/<NAME>.md` |
| Skill / agent instructions | `./.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` |
| Cursor rules | `./.cursor/rules/<scope>.mdc` |

When creating or moving a `.md` file:
- If it documents the project → put it in `docs/`.
- If the doc is for a past phase and no longer maintained → put it in `docs/archive/`.
- Never create `*.md` at repo root other than `README.md`. If asked to, propose the `docs/` location first.

## 3. Backend folder layout (`backend/`)

```
backend/
├── src/
│   ├── config/         # db.js, env loader, third-party config
│   ├── middleware/     # auth, rbac, errorHandler, xss, rateLimit
│   ├── routes/         # one file per resource group (auth, products, sales, …)
│   ├── controllers/    # thin handlers calling services
│   ├── services/       # business logic + DB queries (parameterized only)
│   ├── utils/          # response.js, logger.js, validators
│   └── app.js          # Express app composition
│   └── server.js       # entry point (graceful shutdown)
├── database/           # *.sql scripts (schema, seed) — committed
├── .env                # local secrets — gitignored
├── .env.example        # committed template
└── package.json
```

Naming:
- Files: `camelCase.js` (e.g. `authService.js`, `errorHandler.js`).
- Route files: plural resource name (`products.js`, `sales.js`).
- SQL scripts: `NN_description.sql` numbered in execution order (`01_create_tables.sql`).

## 4. Frontend folder layout (`frontend/`)

```
frontend/src/
├── api/                # axios instance + endpoint wrappers
├── components/         # shared UI (group by domain: ui/, layout/, forms/)
│   ├── ui/             # generic primitives (Button, Input, Modal)
│   └── layout/         # Header, Sidebar, ProtectedRoute
├── contexts/           # React contexts (Auth, Theme, …)
├── pages/              # route-level screens, grouped by feature
│   ├── auth/
│   ├── dashboard/
│   └── <feature>/
├── hooks/              # custom hooks (useAuth, useDebounce, …)
├── services/           # client-side service wrappers calling api/
├── utils/              # format.js, constants.js, helpers
├── router/             # route definitions
├── App.jsx
└── main.jsx
```

Naming:
- Components: `PascalCase.jsx` (e.g. `LoginForm.jsx`, `DashboardPage.jsx`).
- Hooks: `useXxx.js` in `hooks/`.
- Pages: `XxxPage.jsx` colocated with feature folder.
- One default export per component file.

## 5. Where to put a new file (decision tree)

When the user asks to "add/create/write a file":
1. Is it documentation (`.md`)? → use Section 2.
2. Is it backend code?
   - HTTP handler / route → `backend/src/routes/`
   - Business logic / DB query → `backend/src/services/`
   - Request middleware → `backend/src/middleware/`
   - Pure helper → `backend/src/utils/`
3. Is it frontend code?
   - Screen reachable by URL → `frontend/src/pages/<feature>/<NamePage>.jsx`
   - Reusable visual → `frontend/src/components/ui/`
   - Layout chrome → `frontend/src/components/layout/`
   - API call → `frontend/src/api/` (axios) or `frontend/src/services/`
   - React state shared across tree → `frontend/src/contexts/`
   - Reusable hook → `frontend/src/hooks/`
4. Is it a Cursor rule? → `.cursor/rules/<scope>.mdc`.
5. If ambiguous → ASK before creating.

## 6. Files that must NEVER be created at repo root

- `*.md` other than `README.md` (use `docs/`).
- `.env` (use `backend/.env`; commit only `.env.example`).
- Source code of any kind (always under `backend/src` or `frontend/src`).
- `node_modules/` (already gitignored; never edit there).

## 7. When refactoring / moving files

If you move a file, you MUST also:
- Update every relative import path that referenced the old location.
- Update every markdown link (including in `README.md` and other docs).
- Run a quick grep for the old filename to confirm no dangling references.

## 8. Response style

- When proposing where to put a new file, state the path explicitly (e.g. "I'll add it at `backend/src/services/productService.js`") before writing.
- If the user requests a location that violates these rules, push back briefly and propose the correct path.
